# Python bytecode. The fixer and the tooling import modules from tools/p2w-bench on every run, so
# __pycache__ appears within minutes of any work and is never wanted. Two .pyc files were committed
# once and are removed below; leaving them tracked means the tree is permanently dirty, which breaks
# `git pull --rebase` with "please commit or stash them" - which happened on nine consecutive pushes
# today, and every one of them was this and not the fixer's work.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
